# Reference scenario "intro-no-card", US version (GGTE01): title screen -> New Game -> no memory card ->
# continue without saving -> 3D introduction (first dialogue, which waits for A).
# Same logical scenario as games/chibi-robo/scenarios/intro-no-card.scn (PAL), with US-specific frame numbers
# (no 50/60 Hz prompt, shorter boot and loads). Checkpoint names shared by both versions designate the
# same screen in each.
# Format: tools/scenario.py (times in PRESENTED FRAMES, numbered from 1; no game data here).
# Written on GGTE01 with the last build that still emulated the hardware (kept outside this repository's public
# history; cycle clock, RTC 800000000, fixed seed from game.toml [run.force]); its reference run is now recorded
# natively. The checkpoints are on screens that wait for an input, except "loading" (simulated disc read time:
# soft, never makes the comparator fail).
name intro-no-card
description Title screen, New Game, no memory card, continue without saving, 3D intro (US).
version GGTE01
window 4
env GCRT_CARD=absent   # empty port A: this scenario follows the "no memory card" path (as the emulated build did)

input  450 A       # health and safety warning
input 1600 A       # title screen: New Game
input 1900 A       # no-memory-card message: A goes on without saving
input 2100 LEFT    # prompt to confirm playing without saving: cursor from No (preselected) to Yes
input 2250 A       # confirm Yes -> loading, clock scene, birthday party

check  400 health-warning
check 1500 title-screen
check 1800 no-card
check 2060 continue-without-saving
check 2200 yes-selected
check 2330 loading soft
check 3000 birthday-dialogue

end 3150
